     6	 *  - state changes only on a fully accepted write; undelivered state is re-sent (dirty);
     7	 *  - non-EAGAIN errors throttle retries to a 100 ms tick (no spin on an unbound gadget);
     8	 *  - NEVER hold the fd across gadget teardown: when the stop file exists (gadget.sh router_stop
     9	 *    touches it before any UDC/configfs change) or hid_request_close() was called (SIGUSR1),
    10	 *    send a bounded all-up and close; reopen only after the stop file is gone.
