    16	 * tracked; beyond that leaked, still never closed). Staleness = fstat vs stat (st_dev/st_ino/st_rdev), nlink 0 or
    17	 * path gone, checked every ~1 s and immediately after a fatal write error (ENXIO/ESHUTDOWN/ENODEV/EPIPE/EBADF).
    18	 * A fatal error on a node that is NOT stale closes/reopens nothing: retries stay on the 100 ms hard-error tick.
    19	 * The new node is opened by path with back-off 100 ms doubling to 1 s (reset only after a delivered report), then
    20	 * all-keys-up + the held state. Teardown (stop file / SIGUSR1, i.e. before any UDC/configfs change) closes the
    21	 * current AND all parked fds - same as the router's SIGTERM at teardown. Limitation: if mk20-kbd dies while the
    22	 * gadget stays up with a parked fd, hidg0 stays unopenable until the next re-bind or reboot (it keeps retrying). */
