3911:- `mk20-kbd --run`: single-threaded poll loop over ttyS1 and the host tty (`/dev/ttyGS0`, which the PTY↔TCP bridge symlinks; reopened after EIO/EOF). `--no-host` = local mode: pressed key panel turns white, released redraws idle.
3919:- **Per-bus writer threads:** one thread per SPI bus (bus 0: fb1–9 + fb21, bus 1: fb10–20). Producers only copy into `pending` under the bus mutex; the writer snapshots a panel under the lock and writes+fsyncs unlocked. Latest content wins per panel; a panel re-dirtied during its write is written again (unless it went back to the written content); a failing fb is retried with a 200 ms back-off; stop = bounded drain or immediate. Tests: producer never blocked (40 updates with 200 ms writes < 60 ms), coalescing, re-dirty, parallel buses, missing fb, shutdown variants; whole suite also under TSan (`make -C deck/kbd tsan`, part of `make test`).
3957:  - `router_stop` ends with `kbd_hid_quiesce`: SIGUSR1 to validated `bin/mk20-kbd --run` pids, wait until no `/proc/<pid>/fd` points at `/dev/hidg0` (≤3 s), else SIGTERM, then SIGKILL.
