8301:4. **Blocking host replies can deadlock the bridge and prevent modifier release.** [mk20_kbd.c:89](/Users/dev/worktrees/mk20-review-kdr/deck/kbd/mk20_kbd.c:89) enables blocking writes; [kbd.c:35](/Users/dev/worktrees/mk20-review-kdr/deck/kbd/kbd.c:35) writes replies synchronously on the GD32/HID thread. Pipelined valid `getInfo` requests can fill both PTY directions: the bridge blocks writing requests while the daemon blocks writing replies. GD32 releases and HID quiescence stop being serviced; EINTR is retried even after SIGTERM. **Minimal fix:** use nonblocking host output with a bounded queue and timeout, keep HID servicing independent, and honor stop requests during transmission.
