codex
The kernel source confirms a gap in teardown detection: a killed main thread can lose its cmdline while a framebuffer worker remains in uninterruptible I/O and retains shared file descriptors. Both stop checks rediscover processes by cmdline, so they can miss that surviving worker. I’m checking the scope of the final findings; C and shell syntax checks pass.
